  "descriptionPlain": "About the Role\n\nHelp organizations turn AI into meaningful business results. \nOpenAI’s Sales teams work directly with customers to identify valuable uses of our technology. Our Partnerships teams work with technology and services partners to develop joint business plans, bring solutions to market, and help more customers adopt AI.\n\n\n\nThis is a talent pool for GTM Sales and Partnerships professionals across customer segments and industries. Whether you build customer relationships, develop alliances, or grow partner ecosystems, you can apply without choosing a specific team or opening. You do not need experience in both sales and partnerships.\n\n\n\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\nDepending on the opportunity, your work may include:\n\n - Developing account or partner strategies, building pipeline, and advancing commercial opportunities from discovery through negotiation and execution.\n\n - Building trusted relationships with customers, partners, executives, and technical teams, and translating their priorities into a clear business case for AI.\n\n - Creating joint business plans and coordinating co-selling, partner enablement, and delivery with internal teams and external partners.\n\n - Supporting customer deployment, adoption, and growth, and tracking forecasts, commercial performance, or partner outcomes relevant to your role.\n\n - Bringing customer, partner, and market insights back to Product, Research, and the wider GTM organization.\n   \n\nYou might thrive in this role if you:\n\n - Have experience in Sales, Partnerships, business development, or a related commercial role, with evidence of customer or partner impact.\n\n - Can build trust across organizations, navigate complex relationships, and communicate credibly with executives and technical teams.\n\n - Bring sound commercial judgment, turn strategy into practical plans, and stay close to execution and measurable outcomes.\n\n - Are curious about AI, learn quickly, and take ownership in a fast-changing environment.\n\n\nShare your resume and the kinds of opportunities that interest you. Our recruiting team reviews this pool to identify potential matches and may contact you to explore where your background could fit. \nNote: *This is a general expression of interest rather than a specific vacancy, and we may not be able to respond to every application.\n\n\n\nAbout OpenAI\n\nOpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. \n\nWe are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. \n\nFor additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement https://cdn.openai.com/policies/eeo-policy-statement.pdf.\n\nBackground checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations.\n\nTo notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form https://form.asana.com/?d=57018692298241&k=5MqR40fZd7jlxVUh5J-UeA. No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link https://form.asana.com/?k=bQ7w9h3iexRlicUdWRiwvg&d=57018692298241.\n\nOpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy https://cdn.openai.com/policies/global-employee-and-contractor-privacy-policy.pdf\n\nAt OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology."
